### Phone Configurator Simulator — "under the UI" HTTP examples
### Use with the VS Code "REST Client" extension (Huy Nguyen), or copy the
### equivalent curl commands shown in each comment.
###
### Replace @baseUrl with your deployment's /exec URL, e.g.:
### https://script.google.com/macros/s/AKfycb.../exec
###
### Every response is JSON: { "ok": true, "data": {...} } on success,
### or { "ok": false, "error": "..." } on failure.

@baseUrl = https://script.google.com/macros/s/REPLACE_WITH_YOUR_DEPLOYMENT_ID/exec
@email = student01@example.com

### Get current UI config (level, requiredEmailDomain, studentResetEnabled,
### and allowBuyWithPartialConfig — the one bug flag exposed to the client)
# curl "{{baseUrl}}?action=getUiConfig"
GET {{baseUrl}}?action=getUiConfig

### Calculate price for a full configuration (GET, read-only)
# curl "{{baseUrl}}?action=calculate&email=student01%40example.com&model=Pixel%209&storage=128GB&color=Black&network=5G&accessory=None"
GET {{baseUrl}}?action=calculate&email={{email}}&model=Pixel 9&storage=128GB&color=Black&network=5G&accessory=None

### Calculate price for a partial configuration (missing fields price at $0)
GET {{baseUrl}}?action=calculate&email={{email}}&model=Pixel 9&storage=128GB

### Calculate price with a discount code (returns "Unknown code" unless
### it's a real, unused, non-returned code generated for this email — see
### the Buy flow below for how to get one)
GET {{baseUrl}}?action=calculate&email={{email}}&model=Pixel 9&storage=128GB&color=Black&network=5G&accessory=None&discountCode=ABCDEFG

### Get a student's Return-button eligibility and store credit balance
GET {{baseUrl}}?action=getStudentStatus&email={{email}}

### ==== Discount code lifecycle walkthrough ====
### Run these in order against a fresh @email (or after a teacher reset)
### to see the full single-use / return-invalidation behavior (§6.4 of the
### requirements doc).

### 1) Buy with no discount code. The response's data.generatedCode is the
###    new code (Level 2+) — copy it into @generatedCode below.
POST {{baseUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "action": "buy",
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "model": "Pixel 9",
  "storage": "128GB",
  "color": "Black",
  "network": "5G",
  "accessory": "None"
}

### 2) Paste the code from step 1's response here.
@generatedCode = REPLACE_WITH_CODE_FROM_STEP_1

### 3) Buy again using that code — 15% off applies. Note data.generatedCode
###    is null this time: a purchase that itself used a valid code doesn't
###    generate a new one (its own "generatedCode: null" is what the UI
###    shows as "No discount codes for discounted purchases").
POST {{baseUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "action": "buy",
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "model": "Pixel 9 Pro",
  "storage": "256GB",
  "color": "Blue",
  "network": "4G",
  "accessory": "Case",
  "discountCode": "{{generatedCode}}"
}

### 4) Try the same code again — default behavior (allowDiscountCodeReuse
###    off) rejects it: data.discountCode.message = "This code was already
###    used".
GET {{baseUrl}}?action=calculate&email={{email}}&model=Pixel 9&storage=128GB&color=Black&network=5G&accessory=None&discountCode={{generatedCode}}

### 5) Return the phone from step 1 (the one that generated this code) for
###    a refund — this also disables its code.
POST {{baseUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "action": "return",
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "model": "Pixel 9",
  "storage": "128GB",
  "color": "Black",
  "network": "5G",
  "accessory": "None",
  "refundType": "Refund"
}

### 6) A fresh code generated by a *since-returned* purchase reads as
###    disabled instead of merely "used" — message = "Invalid code. The
###    phone that got you this code was returned." (Only meaningful for a
###    code whose own purchase was returned, not the one reused in step 4.)

### Return a phone for store credit (Level 4)
POST {{baseUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "action": "return",
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "model": "Pixel 9 Pro",
  "storage": "256GB",
  "color": "Blue",
  "network": "4G",
  "accessory": "Case",
  "refundType": "StoreCredit"
}

### Reset a student's own data (must be enabled by the teacher)
POST {{baseUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "action": "resetStudent",
  "email": "{{email}}"
}

### ---- Teacher actions (require the teacher password) ----

@teacherPassword = teacher123

### Read current settings
GET {{baseUrl}}?action=teacherGetSettings&password={{teacherPassword}}

### Update settings (full object; unspecified fields are merged over current settings)
POST {{baseUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "action": "teacherUpdateSettings",
  "password": "{{teacherPassword}}",
  "settings": {
    "level": 4,
    "requiredEmailDomain": "",
    "studentResetEnabled": true,
    "bugs": {
      "discountCodeMode": "normal",
      "allowBuyWithPartialConfig": false,
      "returnStaysAvailableWhenEmpty": false,
      "creditBasis": "paid",
      "allowDiscountCodeReuse": false
    }
  }
}

### Toggle on "allow discount code reuse" only (partial update — merges
### over whatever else is currently set)
POST {{baseUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "action": "teacherUpdateSettings",
  "password": "{{teacherPassword}}",
  "settings": {
    "bugs": {
      "allowDiscountCodeReuse": true
    }
  }
}

### Wipe all simulator data (Purchases, DiscountCodes, StoreCredit, ActionLog)
POST {{baseUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "action": "teacherResetAll",
  "password": "{{teacherPassword}}"
}
